    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d10">

                <pb facs="0082" n="8" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg8"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/3683a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-03T15:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 3, 1917, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4631. Crawford<anchor n="2" xml:id="d10-f1"/> of British Embassy informally
                    discussed subject of cooperation with Secretary of Treasury and has reported to
                    his Government. Suggestion was made that there be committees here to handle
                    shipping, munitions, and finances. Department can take no formal steps until
                    Congress has acted.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d10-f1" n="2" xml:id="d10-f1-content">
                <p> Sir Richard Crawford, Commercial Adviser.</p>
            </note>
